! **Two iron moments held 90 degrees apart, with no spin-orbit coupling**: the
! robust magnet `MAGNETISM-NEXT.md` item B asked for, on which a per-atom
! feedback field can be told apart from a penalty (`PLAN.md` P108).
!
! Simple cubic with iron at 0 and (1/2, 1/2, 1/2), which is bcc iron in its
! conventional cell, on the scalar-relativistic ultrasoft `Fe.pz-nd-rrkjus.UPF`
! of `benchmarks/fe-mag-1k.in`. Without spin-orbit coupling nothing but exchange
! acts between the two moments, and exchange wants them parallel: seeded
! parallel this cell is a ferromagnet at 1.868 mu_B per site, and seeded at 90
! degrees with nothing holding it the pair turns parallel (or, from a 1 mu_B
! seed, loses its moment altogether). So holding 90 degrees costs a real
! torque, 0.03 Ry of field per atom, which is what makes the cell a test of a
! controller: the hydrogen pair of `h2-texture-120.in` carries 0.000235 mu_B
! unconstrained, so its `m(B)` is nearly a step and no fixed-gain loop can be
! stable against it.
!
! The same cell in Elk (`tools/cluster/b_elk_fsm.sbatch`, `fsmtype -2`, Elk's
! default `taufsm` and mixer) holds the 90 degrees in 55 loops under a field of
! 0.0097 Ha per atom, which is the external number the scheme here is held to.
!
! No constraint is set here: the tests add the scheme, and the STARTING_MOMENTS
! card that carries the targets.
 &control
    calculation = 'scf'
 /
 &system
    ibrav = 1, celldm(1) = 5.42, nat = 2, ntyp = 1,
    ecutwfc = 25.0, ecutrho = 200.0,
    occupations = 'smearing', smearing = 'marzari-vanderbilt', degauss = 0.05
    noncolin = .true.
    nosym = .true.
    starting_magnetization(1) = 0.5
    angle1(1) = 90.0
    angle2(1) = 0.0
 /
 &electrons
    mixing_beta = 0.3
    conv_thr = 1.0d-8
 /
ATOMIC_SPECIES
 Fe 55.847 Fe.pz-nd-rrkjus.UPF
ATOMIC_POSITIONS (alat)
 Fe 0.00 0.00 0.00
 Fe 0.50 0.50 0.50
K_POINTS {automatic}
 2 2 2 1 1 1
